From: alfcsuarez <alfonsoc.suarez@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] mediatek: hnat: avoid softirq neighbour FOE table scan stalls

Commit porting the 24.10 network baseline reverted the asynchronous
neighbour workqueue and moved foe_clear_entry() synchronously inside
nf_hnat_netevent_handler(), scanning all PPE * foe_etry_num entries
(up to 98,304 descriptors) on every NETEVENT_NEIGH_UPDATE event while
acquiring hnat_account_clear_snapshot() spinlocks before checking BIND.
With frequent IPv4/IPv6 neighbour transitions on active LAN/WAN
interfaces, this stalled softirq execution for 50-250 ms per transition.

Fix this by:
1. Moving IPv4 neighbour FOE invalidation out of softirq into an ordered
   workqueue ("hnat_neigh") with 20 ms batching, same-IP coalescing,
   AF_INET / init_net / NUD_CONNECTED|NUD_FAILED filtering, Ethernet MAC
   bounds check, and periodic cond_resched().
2. Pre-filtering unbound FOE slots locklessly with hnat_entry_peek_bind()
   before invoking hnat_account_clear_snapshot() in foe_clear_entry_batch(),
   entry_delete_by_mac_body(), foe_clear_ethdev_bind_entries(),
   foe_clear_all_bind_entries_body(), and foe_clear_crypto_entry(),
   preserving all HNAT accounting generation fences and fixing snapshot
   pointer shadowing on fallback invalidation.
3. Fixing 6-byte MAC comparison with memcmp(), hoisting PPE cache flushes
   outside inner FOE loops, and initializing/draining the workqueue cleanly
   across probe, warm init, and remove paths.

